            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>Methods and devices to monitor an analyte in body fluid are provided. Embodiments include continuous or discrete acquisition of analyte related data from a transcutaneously positioned in vivo analyte sensor automatically or upon request from a user. The detection and/or monitoring of glucose levels or other analytes, such as lactate, oxygen, AIC, or the like, in certain individuals is vitally important to their health. For example, the monitoring of glucose is particularly important to individuals with diabetes.</p>
            </abstract>
